'''''Lysimachia mauritiana''''' is a species of flowering plant in the primrose family [[Primulaceae]]. It is native to eastern Asia, where it is widespread in coastal areas,<ref name=FoC>[http://www.efloras.org/florataxon.aspx?flora_id=2&taxon_id=200017047 ''Lysimachia mauritiana''] Flora of China</ref> including China, Japan, Korea, Taiwan, the Philippines, and various islands in the Indian and Pacific Ocean.<ref name=FoC/> It is considered to be a common species in Japan.<ref name=Ohwi>{{cite book |last=Ohwi |first=Jisaburo |date=1965 |title=Flora of Japan |url= |location= |publisher=Smithsonian Institution |page=718|isbn= |author-link= }}</ref>   Its natural habitat is along beaches and maritime rock crevices.<ref name=FoC/>

It is a biennial, growing to 50&nbsp;cm tall. It has fleshy spathulate to obovate leaves. It produces white terminal racemes of flowers in late spring and early summer.<ref name=FoC/><ref name=Ohwi/>

